dialogue trust_sage_1
title: The cord
trigger: Trust sage level=1
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The camp is asleep. At the back of the wagon, where the Sage sleeps nearest the satchel, a lantern is still lit, and the Sage is turning a length of knotted cord through both hands.
  * Still mending, this late? -> mending
    do: AddTrust $with 4
  * Put the lantern out. It can be seen from the ridge. -> lantern
    do: AddTrust $with -2
  * Couldn't sleep either. Mind the company? -> company
    do: AddTrust $with 5

node mending hero
  Not mending. Nothing to mend tonight, for once. I'm counting.
  -> cord

node lantern hero
  It's Lantern Road oil. It burns low and it doesn't carry. Sit down, if you're up. I'm counting.
  -> cord

node company hero
  The company's welcome. The counting isn't much to watch, but sit.
  -> cord

node cord commander
  The cord is old and dark with handling. Every finger's width or so there is a knot, pulled tight, and there are a great many of them.
  -> knots

node knots hero
  One knot for every pilgrim who climbed the stair under the spire and didn't come down. I told you I counted them. I didn't say I counted them like this.
  -> why

node why hero
  On the Lantern Road, when somebody dies far from home, the healer who saw them last ties a knot and carries it back to their lantern. So the road knows. Nobody carries these back. So I carry them.
  -> us

node us hero
  Here's what keeps me up, Commander. We're going up that stair. On the road, you tie the knot before the climb, not after, so nobody's forgotten if it goes wrong. Do I tie knots for us?
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Sage holds out the free end of the cord, the part with no knots in it yet.
  * Tie one for each of us. If we don't come down, someone should know. -> tie
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag sage:cord_tied
  * No knots for us. We're coming down, and you're coming with us. -> down
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag sage:cord_down
  * Put the cord away. Counting the dead won't mend anyone. -> away
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag sage:cord_away

node tie hero
  Honest. Most people want me to say it'll be fine. I'll tie them loose, then. A loose knot can come undone on the way back down.
  -> close_line

node down hero
  Coming down. You say it like you've already been up and back. I'll hold you to it. The end of this cord stays clean until you prove me wrong.
  -> close_line

node away hero
  It doesn't mend anyone. You're right about that much. But it isn't for mending. It's so somebody remembers they were here. I'll keep it, Commander. I'll just keep it where you don't have to look at it.
  -> close_line

node close_line hero
  Go and sleep. Somebody bled today and somebody will bleed tomorrow, and I'd like the both of us awake for it.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Sage winds the cord round one wrist, three turns, and blows the lantern out.
